      "role": "user",
      "content": "can u explain the difference between high glycemic index foods and low glycemic index foods? also why does it matter for insulin?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "High glycemic index (GI) foods break down quickly into sugar, causing a rapid spike in blood glucose and a subsequent sharp insulin release to manage it. Low GI foods digest more slowly, leading to a gradual increase in blood sugar and a steadier, lower insulin secretion. This matters because insulin panics to regulate sudden sugar spikes, which can lead to lasting high blood sugar levels (hyperglycemia). Consequently, insulin works harder over time to clear excessive sugar, potentially leading to insulin resistance and increasing the risk of developing type 2 diabetes.",
